35 Residents of Building 28, Niansi San Village v. Yangzhou City Planning Bureau — Administrative Licensing Infringement Case

[ Ruling Summary ]

Where the competent planning administrative authority of a city with zoned district plans, in accordance with the authorization of laws and local regulations, approves a construction project, even if such construction shortens the original sunlight hours of neighboring residences, if it meets the minimum sunlight standards prescribed by the technical specifications of the national and local competent administrative departments, and does not violate other laws or regulations, the approval act shall be deemed lawful.

Plaintiffs: 35 residents of Building 28, Niansi San Village, Yangzhou City, Jiangsu Province (list omitted).

Litigation Representatives: Cao Yuxin, cadre of Yangzhou City Bureau of Justice, Jiangsu Province.

Litigation Representatives: Zhu Yuzhong, worker of Yangzhou City Switch Factory, Jiangsu Province.

Defendant: Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, Jiangsu Province. Address: Middle Wenchang Road, Yangzhou City.

Legal Representative: Zhang Jie, Director of the Bureau.

Third Party: Yangzhou Dongfang Tianyu Real Estate Co., Ltd., Jiangsu Province. Address: Yangzi North Road, Yangzhou City.

Legal Representative: Yu Zhenfei, Chairman of the Company.

On July 7, 2003, the Defendant, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau of Jiangsu Province, in accordance with Article 32 of the *Urban Planning Law of the People's Republic of China* (hereinafter referred to as the Urban Planning Law), issued the Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003076 to the Third Party, Yangzhou Dongfang Tianyu Real Estate Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as Dongfang Tianyu Company), permitting the company to construct Building No. 11-6, the central group, within the Yangzhou Baihe Garden residential complex, with specifications of "nine stories (partially ten stories), residential area of 10,022.2 square meters, attic area of 753 square meters, and height of 26.5 meters." The Plaintiffs, Cao Yuxin and 34 other residents of Building 28 (hereinafter referred to as the Building 28 residents), believed that this planning approval infringed upon their lawful rights and interests, and thus filed an administrative lawsuit with the Yangzhou Intermediate People's Court of Jiangsu Province.

Plaintiffs' Allegations: The Defendant approved the construction of the high-rise residential building No. 11-6 in front of the building where we reside. Together with the buildings No. 11-4 and No. 11-5 permitted under the Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003077 issued by the Defendant to the Third Party, these buildings form a barrier, destroying the landscape of the Slender West Lake scenic area. This does not conform to the urban planning of Yangzhou City, seriously affects our living environment, and infringes upon our lawful rights and interests. We request the revocation of the Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003076 issued by the Defendant.

Main evidence submitted by the Plaintiffs:

1. Certificate from the Owners' Management Committee of Zhengwen Courtyard, Niansi San Village, Yangzhou City, to prove the Plaintiffs' standing to sue.

2. Advertisement for "Oriental Baihe Garden" on Page A4 of *Yangzhou Daily* dated January 10, 2003; six photographs of the Yangzhou Slender West Lake scenic area taken on November 12, 2003; and New Year greeting cards of the "Slender West Lake" scenery from the Yangzhou Municipal People's Government, to prove that the high-rise residential building No. 11-6 approved by the Defendant would affect the landscape of the Yangzhou Slender West Lake scenic area.

Defendant's Defense: On May 6, 2003, Dongfang Tianyu Company, holding the project approval documents, land use certificates, and other documents, applied for the issuance of a construction project planning permit for the second phase of the 11th Group of the Oriental Baihe Garden project. After fulfilling procedures such as providing planning and design conditions, reviewing the design scheme, and reviewing the construction drawings, our bureau issued Construction Project Planning Permits No. 2003076 and No. 2003077 on July 7, 2003, permitting Dongfang Tianyu Company to construct three mid-to-high-rise residential buildings. The main evidence and procedures for this approval fully comply with the Urban Planning Law and the *Jiangsu Province Measures for Implementing the Urban Planning Law* (hereinafter referred to as the Jiangsu Urban Planning Measures) promulgated by the Standing Committee of the Jiangsu Provincial People's Congress. The specific administrative act of our bureau approving the construction project planning of Dongfang Tianyu Company has sufficient main evidence, complies with statutory procedures, and does not infringe upon the Plaintiffs' neighboring rights. The building spacing between the three mid-to-high-rise residential buildings approved by our bureau for the Third Party and the Plaintiffs' building fully meets the requirements of the national *Code for Urban Residential Area Planning and Design* and the *Jiangsu Province Urban Planning Management Technical Regulations*. Specifically, the shading point of Building No. 6 is 26.40 meters high, subtracting a height difference of 1.20 meters, resulting in 25.20 meters. The current distance between Building No. 6 and the Plaintiffs' Building 28 is 34.40 meters, with a sunlight spacing ratio of 1:1.365. Building No. 4 is not directly adjacent to Building 28, and the distance between Building No. 5 and Building 28 reaches 62.7 meters. Therefore, the Plaintiffs' claim that our bureau's administrative approval act seriously affects their living environment and infringes upon their lawful rights and interests has no factual or legal basis.

Main evidence provided by the Defendant:

1. *Minutes of the 14th Meeting of the Yangzhou City Planning Committee* (excerpt);
2. *Regulatory Detailed Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area*;
3. *Report on Balloon Testing of Building Heights at Oriental Baihe Garden*, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, January 5, 2001;
4. *Notice on Expanding the Planning Scope of the Oriental Baihe Garden Residential Area and Issuing Planning and Design Conditions for Its Construction Land*, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, Document No. (2001) 006, January 15, 2001;
5. *Minutes of the 16th Meeting of the City Planning Committee* (excerpt);
6. *Minutes of the Expert Review Meeting on the Planning and Design Scheme of the Oriental Baihe Garden Residential Area and Other Projects*, Expert Panel Review Opinion No. 10 of the Yangzhou City Planning Committee;
7. *Reply on Land Acquisition and Supply for the Construction of Commercial Housing by Dongfang Tianyu Real Estate Co., Ltd.*, Yangzhou City Bureau of Land and Resources, Document No. (2002) Dijiao Zi No. 12, August 30, 2002;
8. *Report on the Second Balloon Testing of Building Heights for the "Oriental Baihe Garden" Project*, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, October 30, 2002;
9. *Notice on the Development and Construction Plan for the Commercial Housing of the Central Plaza, Phase III of the Oriental Baihe Garden Project*, Yangzhou City Development and Planning Commission, Document No. (2002) No. 355, October 31, 2002;
10. *Report on Applying for the Approval of the Central High-Rise Construction Planning Permit for "Oriental Baihe Garden"*, Dongfang Tianyu Company, May 6, 2003;
11. Two *Records of Engineering Location Survey* by Yangzhou Institute of Surveying and Mapping, July 2, 2003;
12. *Measurement of Height Difference between the Proposed Residential Building in the Oriental Baihe Garden and the Existing Residential Building to the North*, and *Calculation Description of the Distance between Part of Slender West Lake, Part of Pingshan Hall, and Part of Oriental Baihe Garden*, Yangzhou Institute of Surveying and Mapping, July 4, 2003;
13. *Notice of Construction Project Location*, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, and *Approval Sheet for Construction Project Line Verification*, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, and Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003076, July 7, 2003;
14. *Description of Building No. 6* and *Sunlight Diagram for Building No. 6*, Yangzhou Hongsha Architectural Design Institute;
15. *Reply of the Provincial Government on the Overall Urban Planning of Yangzhou City*, Jiangsu Provincial People's Government, Document Su Zheng Fu [1999] No. 128, November 16, 1999;
16. *Text of the Overall Urban Planning of Yangzhou City (1996-2010)*;
17. *Overall Plan for the Shugang-Slender West Lake Scenic and Historic Area* (excerpt);

Third Party's Statement: The three residential buildings that the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau permitted our company to construct are not a single enclosed structure but separate, independent buildings. Therefore, the claim of a "barrier" is unfounded. The layout structure formed by these three buildings and the Plaintiffs' residential building is common in urban planning areas. As long as planning management standards are met, there is no impact on the living environment or infringement of rights. "Living environment" and "lawful rights and interests" are general concepts. The Plaintiffs did not specify in their complaint in what way their "living environment" or "lawful rights and interests" were infringed upon. Their request to revoke Construction Project Planning Permits No. 2003076 and No. 2003077 lacks legal basis.

Evidence provided by the Third Party:

1. *Report on Adjusting the Floor Plan of the Central Mid-to-High-Rise Buildings in "Oriental Baihe Garden"*, Dongfang Tianyu Company;
2. *Notice of Approval of Planning and Design Scheme*, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, Document No. (2002) No. 10;
3. *Reply on the Preliminary Design Documents of Yangzhou Oriental Baihe Garden*, Yangzhou City Development and Planning Commission, Document No. (2002) No. 339.

During court examination of evidence, the Plaintiffs (Building 28 residents) raised objections to the legality and relevance of the Defendant's (Yangzhou City Planning Bureau) evidence item 2. For the Defendant's other evidence, they did not challenge the authenticity, legality, or relevance but raised different litigation claims regarding the legal issues demonstrated by the evidence. The Third Party, Dongfang Tianyu Company, did not object to the evidence presented by the Defendant. The Defendant and the Third Party did not object to the Plaintiffs' evidence item 1. They argued that the Plaintiffs' evidence item 2 was not relevant to the Construction Project Planning Permit issued by the Defendant. The Third Party did not state the evidential content or purpose of the evidence it provided during the litigation, nor did it present or examine this evidence during the court hearing.

The Yangzhou Intermediate People's Court found the following facts of the case:

On November 14, 2000, the Yangzhou City Planning Committee held its 14th meeting. The meeting reviewed the project location determination for expanding the land use scope of Dongfang Tianyu Company on the north side of Oriental Baihe Garden, in conjunction with the approved residential area plan, to support the construction of supporting facilities such as schools and farmers' markets. The project location was agreed in principle, and it was decided to proceed according to the preliminary review opinion of the Planning Bureau, expanding the land use scope east to Yangzi North Road and north to the Niansi River, with unified planning and phased implementation. Subsequently, the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau and the Yangzhou City Urban Planning and Design Institute prepared and reviewed the *Regulatory Detailed Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area*. On December 25, 2000, the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, together with the Yangzhou Development Office, the Yangzhou Municipal Government Affairs Administration, and the Scenic Area Office, conducted a balloon test of the building height at Oriental Baihe Garden. On January 12, 2001, the Yangzhou City Planning Committee held its 16th meeting, heard reports on the building height tests for the mid-to-high-rise residential buildings in the Oriental Baihe Garden project, and agreed in principle with the Planning Bureau's review opinion that "implementation should follow the approved detailed residential area plan, but the roof forms of the individual mid-to-high-rise buildings should be appropriately adjusted by drawing on traditional techniques." It also suggested that the design of the individual mid-to-high-rise buildings should incorporate rooftop gardens to reduce the impact on the scenic area. On January 15, 2001, the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau issued Document No. (2001) 006, *Notice on Expanding the Planning Scope of the Oriental Baihe Garden Residential Area and Issuing Planning and Design Conditions for Its Construction Land*, to the Third Party. On February 26, 2001, the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau convened an expert review meeting on the planning and design schemes for the Oriental Baihe Garden residential area and other projects, producing the *Minutes of the Expert Review Meeting on the Planning and Design Scheme of the Oriental Baihe Garden Residential Area and Other Projects*. On October 26, 2002, the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, together with the Garden Bureau and the Cultural Relics Administration, conducted another balloon test of the building height at Oriental Baihe Garden.

On May 6, 2003, the Third Party, Dongfang Tianyu Company, submitted a *Report on Applying for the Approval of the Central High-Rise Construction Planning Permit for "Oriental Baihe Garden"* to the Defendant, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, and simultaneously provided the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau with the *Reply on Land Acquisition and Supply for the Construction of Commercial Housing by Dongfang Tianyu Real Estate Co., Ltd.* (Document No. (2002) Dijiao Zi No. 12, August 30, 2002, from the Yangzhou City Bureau of Land and Resources); the *Notice on the Development and Construction Plan for the Commercial Housing of the Central Plaza, Phase III of the Oriental Baihe Garden Project* (Document No. (2002) No. 355, October 31, 2002, from the Yangzhou City Development and Planning Commission); and related architectural design drawings. On July 1, 2003, Dongfang Tianyu Company completed the relevant payment procedures for Building No. 11-6 of the Central Group of Oriental Baihe Garden. On July 2, 2003, the Yangzhou Institute of Surveying and Mapping conducted an engineering location survey for the construction project. On July 4, 2003, the Yangzhou Institute of Surveying and Mapping measured the height difference between the proposed residential building in Oriental Baihe Garden and the existing residential building to the north, and calculated the distances between parts of Slender West Lake, parts of Pingshan Hall, and parts of Oriental Baihe Garden. In addition, the Yangzhou Hongsha Architectural Design Institute provided explanations regarding the relevant data of Building No. 11-6 and the sunlight spacing ratio between that building and the adjacent Building 28 to the north. On July 7, 2003, the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau conducted the location and line verification for the construction project of Building No. 11-6 and issued the *Notice of Construction Project Location* and the *Approval Sheet for Construction Project Line Verification* from the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau. On the same day, the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau issued Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003076 to Dongfang Tianyu Company.

The Yangzhou Intermediate People's Court conducted the following review and determinations:

I. Whether the specific administrative act in question infringed upon the Plaintiffs' neighboring rights.

When issuing Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003076, the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau fully considered whether the sunlight of the Plaintiffs (the residents of Building 28) would be affected by reviewing architectural drawings, calculating sunlight spacing ratios, conducting engineering location surveys, and verifying building lines. The calculation showed that the sunlight spacing ratio between Building No. 11-6 and Building 28 was 1:1.365, meeting the minimum requirement of 1:1.2 stipulated in Article 3.1 of the *Jiangsu Province Urban Planning Management Technical Regulations*. The Building 28 residents did not raise any objection during the court hearing that the specific administrative act in question would affect the sunlight of their residential building. Building No. 11-6, together with Building No. 11-4 and Building No. 11-5 permitted under Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003077, formed a triangular layout, with certain spacing in the front, back, left, and right. This type of construction is not prohibited by building technical specifications. The Building 28 residents' claim that the three residential buildings (No. 11-4, No. 11-5, and No. 11-6) formed a 170-meter barrier affecting the ventilation of their residential building lacks support from laws, regulations, or technical specifications. Therefore, the Building 28 residents' claim that their right to ventilation, as a neighboring right, was infringed upon by the specific administrative act in question is unfounded. Their claim that the specific administrative act affected the implementation of the original plan for Building 28 also lacks factual and legal basis.

II. Whether the specific administrative act in question was lawful.

First, whether the procedure of the specific administrative act in question was lawful. The specific administrative act in this case occurred at a stage within the overall construction project of the Oriental Baihe Garden residential area. The Defendant, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, in the overall project approval procedure for this residential area, had already fulfilled the procedures for proposing construction project planning and design conditions and reviewing the project design scheme in accordance with Article 32 of the Urban Planning Law, Article 26 of the Jiangsu Urban Planning Measures, and Article 40 of the *Yangzhou City Urban Planning Management Measures*. This included certain procedures that should have been fulfilled for issuing Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003076, leading to a situation where the time for proposing planning and design conditions and reviewing the project design scheme preceded the time when Dongfang Tianyu Company applied for the permit. This reverse chronological order in procedure was caused by the special nature of the construction project and cannot be deemed to constitute a violation of laws, regulations, or administrative regulations by the specific administrative act.

Second, whether the *Regulatory Detailed Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area* was lawfully and validly approved. Regarding the approval of detailed urban plans, Article 21, Paragraph 8 of the Urban Planning Law and Article 12, Paragraph 8 of the Jiangsu Urban Planning Measures are consistent, stating: "Detailed urban plans shall be approved by the city people's government; for cities that prepare zoned district plans, the detailed plans, except for important ones to be approved by the city people's government, shall be approved by the city people's government's competent urban planning administrative department." In this case, the Defendant, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, provided the *Regulatory Detailed Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area* and the minutes of the 14th and 16th meetings of the Yangzhou City Planning Committee to demonstrate that the *Regulatory Detailed Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area* had been approved by the 16th meeting of the Yangzhou City Planning Committee, with the approval taking the form of meeting minutes. At the same time, the Yangzhou City Planning Bureau also provided the *Yangzhou City Urban Planning Management Measures* to explain the authority and functions of the Yangzhou City Planning Committee. Article 3 of these Measures stipulates that the Yangzhou City Planning Committee, entrusted by the municipal government, is responsible for research, decision-making, organization, implementation, and management of urban planning work; organizing corresponding planning compilation and approval; and coordinating and supervising the implementation of important planning matters. Accordingly, when the Yangzhou municipal government implemented the approval procedures for detailed plans as required by the Urban Planning Law and the Jiangsu Implementation Measures, it authorized the Planning Committee to handle this work. This practice itself is not prohibited by laws or regulations. Whether a detailed urban plan has been lawfully and validly approved should be demonstrated through a certain form of approval. In this case, the approval of the relevant detailed plan took the form of meeting minutes of the City Planning Committee signed by the mayor. Although the statement "implement according to the approved detailed residential area plan" in the minutes of the 16th meeting of the City Planning Committee led to different interpretations among the parties in this case, a comprehensive analysis of the entire content of the evidence, including the minutes of the 14th meeting of the Yangzhou City Planning Committee, the *Regulatory Detailed Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area*, and the minutes of the 16th meeting of the Yangzhou City Planning Committee, leads to the conclusion that the detailed plan was reviewed and approved by the Yangzhou City Planning Committee and then signed for approval by the mayor. As to whether such meeting minutes constitute a common form of approval, since laws and regulations only stipulate that detailed urban plans shall be approved by the city people's government or the competent planning administrative department, without specifying the form of approval, the actual role played by the meeting minutes of the Yangzhou City Planning Committee in approving the detailed plan cannot be denied. Therefore, it must be determined that the *Regulatory Detailed Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area* was lawfully and validly approved. Consequently, the Building 28 residents' litigation claim that the *Regulatory Detailed Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area* was not lawfully and validly approved is untenable.

Third, whether the specific administrative act in question violated the *Overall Plan for the Shugang-Slender West Lake Scenic and Historic Area*. In the review of this case, no circumstances were found in which the specific administrative act violated the *Overall Plan for the Shugang-Slender West Lake Scenic and Historic Area*. Therefore, the Building 28 residents' claim that because the proposed residential building can be seen from the scenic area, it should be deemed to affect the scenic area plan is unfounded.

In summary, the specific administrative act in question has sufficient evidence, lawful procedures, and correct application of law. The Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003076 issued by the Defendant, Yangzhou City Planning Bureau, is lawful. The construction of Building No. 11-6, the central group, in the Oriental Baihe Garden, as approved for the Third Party, Dongfang Tianyu Company, does not infringe upon the neighboring rights, including the right to ventilation, of the Plaintiffs, the residents of Building 28.

据此，扬州市中级人民法院依照最高人民法院《关于执行〈中华人民共和国行政诉讼法〉若干问题的解释》第五十六条第（四）项的规定，于2003年12月10日判决：

驳回原告28幢楼居民要求撤销被告扬州市规划局2003年7月7日核发的扬规建字2003076号《建设工程规划许可证》的诉讼请求。

Accordingly, the Yangzhou Intermediate People's Court, pursuant to paragraph (4) of Article 56 of the Interpretation of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning the Implementation of the Administrative Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, rendered judgment on December 10, 2003, as follows:

The claims of the plaintiffs, the residents of Building 28, for revocation of the Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003076 (Yang Gui Jian Zi [2003] No. 076) issued by the defendant, Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning, on July 7, 2003, are dismissed.

宣判后，28幢楼居民不服，向江苏省高级人民法院提起上诉。

After the judgment was pronounced, the residents of Building 28, being dissatisfied, appealed to the Jiangsu High People's Court.

28幢楼居民的上诉理由是：（1）居住环境应包括通风、采光、日照、噪音、滴水等许多因素，但并非所有因素都有明确的可实际操作的技术规范。扬州市规划局许可东方天宇公司规划建设的11-6号楼，虽然满足住宅日照系数技术规范的要求，考虑了建筑间距，但该幢楼与其许可东方天宇公司规划建设的11-4、11-5号楼形成长达170米的建筑屏障，势必导致前后通风不畅，使得28幢楼居民的居住环境质量下降。故原审判决仅以达到日照间距为由，而不考虑其他因素，认定被诉具体行政行为不构成对上诉人居住环境的影响，没有法律依据；（2）本案所涉地段在扬州市没有分区规划，根据法律规定，该地段的详细规划应由扬州市人民政府审批。原审判决认定扬州市规划委员会有权代表扬州市人民政府对《念泗二村地段控制性详细规划》进行审批，无法律依据。同时，扬州市规划委员会第十四次和第十六次会议纪要的内容均不能证明是对详细规划的审批，原审法院以分析的方法推论该详细规划已经批准，证据不足；（3）扬州市规划局行政行为的次序颠倒，程序违法；（4）扬州市规划局的许可行为破坏了风景区的自然人文景观，违反了《蜀岗一瘦西湖风景名胜区规划》。请求撤销一审判决，撤销2003076号《建设工程规划许可证》。

The grounds of appeal of the residents of Building 28 were as follows: (1) The living environment should include many factors such as ventilation, lighting, sunshine, noise, and dripping water, but not all factors have clear and practically operable technical standards. Although Building 11-6, which the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning permitted Dongfang Tianyu Company to plan and construct, satisfied the technical standard requirements for the residential sunshine coefficient and took building spacing into account, that building, together with Buildings 11-4 and 11-5 which the Bureau also permitted Dongfang Tianyu Company to plan and construct, formed a building barrier extending 170 meters, which would inevitably lead to poor ventilation between the front and back, thereby degrading the quality of the living environment of the residents of Building 28. Therefore, the trial court judgment, which relied solely on the achievement of the sunshine spacing ratio without considering other factors and concluded that the specific administrative act challenged did not constitute an impact on the appellants' living environment, had no legal basis. (2) There was no zoning plan for the area involved in this case in Yangzhou City. According to the law, the detailed plan for that area should be approved by the Yangzhou Municipal People's Government. The trial court judgment's conclusion that the Yangzhou Municipal Planning Committee had the authority to approve, on behalf of the Yangzhou Municipal People's Government, the Detailed Regulatory Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area had no legal basis. Furthermore, the contents of the minutes of the 14th and 16th meetings of the Yangzhou Municipal Planning Committee could not prove that they constituted approval of the detailed plan. The trial court's inference by analytical reasoning that the detailed plan had been approved lacked sufficient evidence. (3) The sequence of administrative actions by the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning was reversed, and the procedures were illegal. (4) The permitting act of the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning damaged the natural and cultural landscape of the scenic area, violating the Shugang-Slender West Lake Scenic Area Plan. The appellants requested that the judgment of first instance be reversed and that Permit No. 2003076 be revoked.

江苏省高级人民法院经审理认为：

The Jiangsu High People's Court, upon trial, held as follows:

本案中的当事人不是具体行政行为的直接相对人，而是因相邻权受到侵害而提起行政诉讼。起诉所基于的相邻权，属于民法范畴。根据《中华人民共和国民法通则》的规定，民事主体因建筑物相邻产生的日照、通风、采光、排水、通行等民事纠纷，应当通过民事诉讼的方式解决。但现实中，如果一方当事人实施的与其他当事人相邻权有关的行为是经行政机关批准、许可的，其他当事人就无法通过民事诉讼获得救济。为此，最高人民法院《关于执行〈中华人民共和国行政诉讼法〉若干问题的解释》第十三条第一款第（二）项规定相邻权人有对行政主体作出的涉及相邻权的具体行政行为提起行政诉讼的原告主体资格，其目的是保护民事主体享有的相邻权不受侵害。本案28幢楼居民因认为扬州市规划局核发给东方天宇公司的2003076号《建设工程规划许可证》侵犯其日照、通风、采光等相邻权而提起行政诉讼。因此，这类行政诉讼的审查重点，应当是被诉具体行政行为许可建设的建筑项目是否符合有关建筑管理的技术规范，是否侵犯了原告的相邻权。

The parties in this case are not the direct counterparts of the specific administrative act, but rather have initiated administrative proceedings because their neighboring rights have been infringed. The neighboring rights on which the lawsuit is based fall within the realm of civil law. According to the provisions of the General Principles of the Civil Law of the People's Republic of China, civil disputes arising from building adjacency, such as those concerning sunshine, ventilation, lighting, drainage, and passage, shall be resolved through civil litigation. However, in practice, if an act implemented by one party that concerns the neighboring rights of another party has been approved or permitted by an administrative authority, the other party cannot obtain relief through civil proceedings. To address this, subparagraph (2) of paragraph 1 of Article 13 of the Interpretation of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning the Implementation of the Administrative Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China provides that a neighboring right holder has the standing as a plaintiff to initiate administrative proceedings against a specific administrative act of an administrative body that involves neighboring rights, for the purpose of protecting the neighboring rights enjoyed by civil subjects from infringement. In this case, the residents of Building 28 initiated administrative proceedings because they believed that the Construction Project Planning Permit No. 2003076 issued by the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning to Dongfang Tianyu Company infringed their neighboring rights to sunshine, ventilation, and lighting. Therefore, the focus of review in such administrative proceedings should be on whether the construction project permitted by the specific administrative act under challenge complies with the relevant technical standards for construction management and whether it infringes the plaintiffs' neighboring rights.

《江苏省城市规划管理技术规定》根据居住建筑日照标准和当地实际情况，确定南京、镇江、扬州（除宝应、高邮外）等地住宅楼的日照间距系数为1：1.2。2003076号《建设工程规划许可证》涉及的百合园小区11-6号住宅楼与28幢楼之间的日照间距比，经测算已达1∶1.365，超过了国家和江苏省有关部门规定的日照间距最低标准，上诉人对此没有异议。因此，虽然扬州市规划局许可东方天宇公司建造的百合园小区11-6号住宅楼缩短了28幢楼的原日照时间，但不构成对28幢楼居民日照权的侵犯。此外，11-6号住宅楼与扬州市规划局另外许可建设的11-4、11-5号住宅楼，在布局上呈由南向北的倒品字形，各楼之间均有一定间距。按照国家标准《城市居住区规划设计规范》的要求和说明，各住宅楼间距的设定，以满足日照要求为基础，并综合考虑采光、通风、消防、防灾、管线埋设、视觉卫生等因素。因此，原审判决认定扬州市规划局的行政许可行为并不影响上诉人享有的法定日照、采光、通风等相邻权，是有事实和法律依据的。28幢楼居民认为上述三幢楼房形成170米的屏障，影响其通风、小区管线埋设等，因无事实和法律依据，故不予采信。原审判决驳回28幢楼居民的诉讼请求，并无不当。

According to the Jiangsu Provincial Urban Planning Management Technical Regulations, in accordance with the sunshine standards for residential buildings and local actual conditions, the sunshine spacing coefficient for residential buildings in areas such as Nanjing, Zhenjiang, and Yangzhou (excluding Baoying and Gaoyou) is set at 1:1.2. The sunshine spacing ratio between Building 11-6 of the Baiheyuan Community, which is the subject of Permit No. 2003076, and Building 28 has been measured at 1:1.365, exceeding the minimum sunshine spacing standard prescribed by the relevant national and Jiangsu provincial authorities, and the appellants do not dispute this fact. Therefore, although the construction of Building 11-6 in the Baiheyuan Community permitted by the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning shortened the original sunshine duration for Building 28, it does not constitute an infringement of the right to sunshine of the residents of Building 28. Furthermore, Building 11-6, together with Buildings 11-4 and 11-5, which were also permitted by the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning, are laid out in an inverted pin-shaped configuration from south to north, with a certain spacing between each building. In accordance with the requirements and explanatory notes of the national standard, the Code for Planning and Design of Urban Residential Areas, the setting of spacing between residential buildings is based on satisfying sunshine requirements and takes into comprehensive consideration factors such as lighting, ventilation, fire protection, disaster prevention, pipeline laying, and visual hygiene. Therefore, the trial court's judgment that the administrative licensing act of the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning did not affect the statutory neighboring rights of the appellants to sunshine, lighting, and ventilation had a factual and legal basis. The contention of the residents of Building 28 that the three buildings formed a 170-meter barrier affecting their ventilation and the laying of community pipelines is not supported by facts or law and is therefore not accepted. The trial court's dismissal of the claims of the residents of Building 28 was not improper.

本案中，上诉人28幢楼居民在一审是以东方天宇公司依被上诉人扬州市规划局批准建设的两幢高层住宅楼侵犯其相邻权为由，提出撤销2003076号《建设工程规划许可证》的诉讼请求。故原审法院根据行政诉讼法的规定，对扬州市规划局核发的2003076号《建设工程规划许可证》的程序是否合法、所依据的《念泗二村地段详细规划》是否经过合法批准，以及是否违反《蜀岗一瘦西湖风景名胜区总体规划》，是否符合法律规定进行审查。查明东方天宇公司已按有关法律规定向扬州市规划局提交了建设申请、建设项目批准文件、建设用地证件、设计方案、施工图等材料，扬州市规划局在依法对上述材料进行审查的基础上，核发了2003076号《建设工程规划许可证》。由此认定扬州市规划局核发的2003076号《建设工程规划许可证》，符合有关法律规定，并未侵犯28幢楼居民的合法权益，并无不妥。

In this case, the appellants, the residents of Building 28, filed their claim in the first instance on the ground that two high-rise residential buildings constructed by Dongfang Tianyu Company pursuant to the approval of the appellee, the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning, infringed their neighboring rights, and sought revocation of Permit No. 2003076. Accordingly, the trial court, in accordance with the provisions of the Administrative Procedure Law, reviewed whether the procedures for the issuance of Permit No. 2003076 by the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning were lawful, whether the Detailed Plan for the Niansi Er Village Area on which it was based had been lawfully approved, and whether it violated the Overall Plan for the Shugang-Slender West Lake Scenic Area, and complied with legal provisions. The court found that Dongfang Tianyu Company had, in accordance with relevant legal provisions, submitted to the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning materials including a construction application, project approval documents, land use documents for construction, a design plan, and construction drawings. Upon lawfully reviewing the above materials, the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning issued Permit No. 2003076. The court thus concluded that the issuance of Permit No. 2003076 by the Yangzhou Municipal Bureau of Planning complied with relevant legal provisions and did not infringe the lawful rights and interests of the residents of Building 28. This conclusion was not improper.

综上，江苏省高级人民法院依据《中华人民共和国行政诉讼法》第六十一条第（一）项的规定，于2004年3月19日判决：

驳回上诉，维持原判。

In conclusion, the Jiangsu High People's Court, pursuant to paragraph (1) of Article 61 of the Administrative Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, rendered judgment on March 19, 2004, as follows:

The appeal is dismissed and the original judgment is affirmed.
